(:id "port/python/vt/cook-open" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_test.go: TestPythonCook/open" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_test.go: TestPythonCook/negative-controls/reserved" "make python-cook-negative-control (make/python.mk)" "make dist-python") :tested-revision "be236674a4184c00ac4f51942148317f239409f8" :note "2026-11-15: the runtime opens the tool's little-endian cook of a fixed root and of a variable root with a shared pointer tail, and refuses the forged header, directory and region frames by cook-check's names: not_a_cook, foreign_order (a big-endian cook and a reversed magic), wrong_build_version, reserved_not_zero, bad_alignment, truncated, unaligned_base and bad_layout (sentinel, unknown type, descending offsets, root off base, overlap, region escape, misaligned entry, unnamed reference, reference to another type). Open stays match-and-point, so a forged reference or directory entry still opens while Check refuses it. The reserved-word control disables the header check in a copy of _schema/cook.py and the probe goes red. Run on Linux x86-64 with CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 built into dist/ by make dist-python, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
(:id "port/python/vt/cook-write" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_test.go: TestPythonCook/write" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_test.go: TestPythonCook/negative-controls/order, TestPythonCook/negative-controls/wide_order, TestPythonCook/negative-controls/reference_delta, TestPythonCook/negative-controls/attribution_length" "make python-cook-negative-control (make/python.mk)" "make dist-python") :tested-revision "be236674a4184c00ac4f51942148317f239409f8" :note "2026-11-15: Cook writes tablecook.Cook's file byte for byte in both byte orders for a fixed root (a nested fixed table with int8, uint32, int128 and uint128) and a variable root (a pointer chain whose tail a second slot shares), and CookMeasure equals the file length; the little file opens under the runtime and the big file refuses foreign_order on this little-endian host. The write-side controls move the byte order, the wide integer's order, the pointer delta and the attribution length in a copy of _schema/cookwrite.py and each comparison goes red. The runtime covers the constructs the table codec carries (bool, the integers through 128 bits, by-value tables, *T pointers); a field of any other kind refuses by name. Run on Linux x86-64 with CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 built into dist/ by make dist-python, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
